        "answer": {
          "short": "For $x=-2,-1,0,1,2$, the corresponding $y$-values are $-1,-1,\\text{undefined},1,1$. The graph has $y=1$ for $x>0$ and $y=-1$ for $x<0$, with open endpoints at $(0,1)$ and $(0,-1)$.",
          "worked": "Using part a, both negative inputs give $y=-1$ and both positive inputs give $y=1$. At $x=0$ the function is undefined.\n\nDraw the ray $y=-1$ to the left of the $y$-axis and the ray $y=1$ to the right. Use open circles at $(0,-1)$ and $(0,1)$ because $x=0$ is excluded.",
